  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "An owner seeking chain distribution and loyalty benefits **without making the property look and operate like a standardized chain hotel** would typically evaluate a **soft brand or collection brand**.\n\n### Commonly considered options in Mexico\n\n| Parent company | Collection/soft brands | Typical positioning |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Marriott** | **Autograph Collection**, **Tribute Portfolio**, **The Luxury Collection**, Design Hotels | Upper-upscale through luxury |\n| **Hilton** | **Curio Collection**, **Tapestry Collection**, **LXR Hotels & Resorts** | Upscale through luxury |\n| **Hyatt** | **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt**, **JdV by Hyatt**, Destination by Hyatt | Lifestyle, upper-upscale and luxury |\n| **IHG** | **Vignette Collection** | Luxury and lifestyle |\n| **Accor** | **MGallery**, **Handwritten Collection**, Emblems Collection | Midscale boutique through luxury |\n| **Wyndham** | **Trademark Collection**, **Registry Collection Hotels** | Upper-midscale through luxury |\n| **Choice/BWH** | Ascend Hotel Collection, BW Premier Collection and selected WorldHotels collections | Midscale through upscale |\n\nThese brands generally let the property retain its **existing name, architecture, design narrative, local food-and-beverage concepts and sense of place**, while accessing the parent company’s reservation system, loyalty program, sales network and technology platform. ([hotel-development.marriott.com](https://www.hotel-development.marriott.com/brands/premium-brands?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Most likely initial shortlist\n\nFor an upscale or luxury independent hotel in Mexico, the most frequent first comparisons would normally be:\n\n1. **Autograph Collection**\n2. **Curio Collection**\n3. **Tribute Portfolio**\n4. **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt**\n5. **The Luxury Collection or LXR** for a genuinely luxury asset\n6. **Tapestry, Trademark or Handwritten Collection** for a less-luxury, more conversion-oriented property\n\nThese are locally relevant choices: Marriott already lists Autograph and Tribute properties in Mexico; Hyatt has used Unbound in San Miguel de Allende; Hilton is expanding Tapestry in La Paz; and Wyndham’s Registry portfolio includes Mexican resort properties. ([marriott.com](https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotel-sitemap/mexico-hotel-sitemap?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf the owner wants **still greater independence and fewer operating standards**, representation organizations such as **Preferred Hotels & Resorts, The Leading Hotels of the World, Small Luxury Hotels of the World or Relais & Châteaux** may also be considered, although these operate differently from a conventional franchise or management-company soft brand. ([lodgingmagazine.com](https://lodgingmagazine.com/the-independent-hotels-guide-to-soft-brands/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThe best fit ultimately depends on the hotel’s **ADR, room count, resort versus urban location, existing identity, renovation requirements, loyalty-program contribution and total affiliation fees**. “Soft” branding preserves more individuality, but it does not necessarily mean lower fees or minimal brand standards.",
